They really have you wrapped around their fingers.

278
00:12:36,058 --> 00:12:38,558
No, they aren't those kind of people, okay?

279
00:12:38,558 --> 00:12:43,558
Any noble with a criminal record to his name will damage his family's hard-earned reputation.

280
00:12:43,558 --> 00:12:46,058
You would also be barred from entering Hightown.

281
00:12:46,058 --> 00:12:52,058
Those two forced you to leave home and get involved with their atrocious acts of violence against your better judgment.

282
00:12:52,058 --> 00:12:54,058
Isn't that right, Sabo?

283
00:12:56,558 --> 00:12:58,058
Look here, son.

284
00:12:58,058 --> 00:13:01,058
The fate of your friends in Grey Terminal is in the hand of pirates.

285
00:13:01,058 --> 00:13:03,058
Those pirates work for me.

286
00:13:03,058 --> 00:13:05,058
All I need to do is give the order.

287
00:13:05,058 --> 00:13:11,058
If these slum brats are that important, think long and hard about what you have to do.

288
00:13:13,558 --> 00:13:16,558
You're a smart boy, born to a great family.

289
00:13:16,558 --> 00:13:18,558
You already know what's right.

290
00:13:18,558 --> 00:13:20,558
You promised me you wouldn't hurt them.

291
00:13:20,558 --> 00:13:22,558
That's the only reason I came back here.

292
00:13:22,558 --> 00:13:24,558
You haven't changed at all since I ran away.

293
00:13:24,558 --> 00:13:26,558
No one tempted me.

294
00:13:26,558 --> 00:13:29,558
I made every decision by my own free will.

295
00:13:32,558 --> 00:13:34,558
You disappoint me.

296
00:13:34,558 --> 00:13:36,558
I apologize, sir.

297
00:13:36,558 --> 00:13:39,558
I'm so ashamed that I have such a foolish son.

298
00:13:39,558 --> 00:13:41,558
Surely you understand my dilemma.

299
00:13:41,558 --> 00:13:42,558
Of course.

300
00:13:42,558 --> 00:13:45,558
It must tear you apart inside.

301
00:13:45,558 --> 00:13:47,558
Don't you worry.

302
00:13:47,558 --> 00:13:49,558
I'll take care of all the paperwork.

303
00:13:49,558 --> 00:14:07,558
Welcome back, sir.

304
00:14:07,558 --> 00:14:09,558
Home at last.

305
00:14:09,558 --> 00:14:10,558
Let's go, Sabo.

306
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:12,558
You've been gone quite some time.

307
00:14:12,558 --> 00:14:15,558
On second thought, don't come in yet.

308
00:14:15,558 --> 00:14:16,558
You must be filthy.

309
00:14:16,558 --> 00:14:20,558
Hose yourself off in the yard first, then come in and take a bath.

310
00:14:20,558 --> 00:14:23,558
We're all glad that you're back home safe, young master.

311
00:14:23,558 --> 00:14:25,558
Oh, goodness!

312
00:14:25,558 --> 00:14:26,558
Is it really you?

313
00:14:26,558 --> 00:14:28,558
You've grown so big.

314
00:14:28,558 --> 00:14:30,558
Hello, Mom.

315
00:14:30,558 --> 00:14:33,558
Now, Steli, say hello to your brother, Sabo.

316
00:14:33,558 --> 00:14:35,558
Nice to meet you, big brother.

317
00:14:35,558 --> 00:14:37,558
I'm Steli and I'm eight.

318
00:14:37,558 --> 00:14:38,558
What about you?

319
00:14:38,558 --> 00:14:42,558
What the hell?

320
00:14:42,558 --> 00:14:43,558
We adopted him.

321
00:14:43,558 --> 00:14:46,558
He's a promising boy from another noble family.

322
00:14:46,558 --> 00:14:50,558
For reasons beyond understanding, his parents suddenly became neglectful.

323
00:14:50,558 --> 00:14:53,558
So far, he's fit in extremely well.

324
00:14:53,558 --> 00:14:58,558
I imagine that if things don't work out with you when it's time to choose a successor, then he would...

325
00:14:58,558 --> 00:15:00,558
No, no, never mind.

326
00:15:00,558 --> 00:15:02,558
I've said too much.

327
00:15:02,558 --> 00:15:04,558
Go and get settled in your room.

328
00:15:04,558 --> 00:15:07,558
You'll resume your studies tomorrow morning.

329
00:15:07,558 --> 00:15:20,558
Are you gonna abandon all your dreams just like that?

330
00:15:20,558 --> 00:15:23,558
Hey, do you know what I heard?

331
00:15:23,558 --> 00:15:26,558
You're dumb as a brick.

332
00:15:26,558 --> 00:15:30,558
That's what Mama and Papa think, in case you couldn't guess.

333
00:15:30,558 --> 00:15:33,558
But still, you sure are lucky.

334
00:15:33,558 --> 00:15:36,558
Tomorrow night, they're taking care of the garbage.

335
00:15:36,558 --> 00:15:43,558
To think had you stayed in Grey Terminal a day longer, you'd be dead like the rest of the crooks.

336
00:15:43,558 --> 00:15:45,558
Too bad.

337
00:15:45,558 --> 00:15:50,558
My life would be a lot easier if you never came back, but I'm clever enough so I'll make do.

338
00:15:50,558 --> 00:15:55,558
Heyo, stop! Let go of me or I'll tell Papa!

339
00:15:55,558 --> 00:15:57,558
What did you say? What's going on?

340
00:15:57,558 --> 00:16:00,558
You tell me everything, or I'll beat you up.

341
00:16:00,558 --> 00:16:03,558
Wait! Tomorrow, there's going to be a fire!

342
00:16:03,558 --> 00:16:05,558
They're burning Grey Terminal!

343
00:16:05,558 --> 00:16:06,558
A fire?

344
00:16:06,558 --> 00:16:07,558
That's right!

345
00:16:07,558 --> 00:16:10,558
You didn't hear about it because you've been away for so long.

346
00:16:10,558 --> 00:16:13,558
The nobles in Hightown decided it months ago.

347
00:16:13,558 --> 00:16:18,558
The world government is sending a group of people to check out all of the East Blue.

348
00:16:19,558 --> 00:16:23,558
They're finally going to arrive and go a kingdom three days from now.

349
00:16:23,558 --> 00:16:28,558
Rumor has it they have a world noble, a celestial dragon with them.

350
00:16:28,558 --> 00:16:34,558
People are panicking. The members of the royal family don't want him to see all the dirty parts of this country.

351
00:16:34,558 --> 00:16:38,558
So they made the obvious decision to burn down Grey Terminal.

352
00:16:38,558 --> 00:16:41,558
It's a surefire way to cleanse this country of all its rubbish.

353
00:16:41,558 --> 00:16:45,558
There's no way they'd just burn everything down without warning!

354
00:16:45,558 --> 00:16:47,558
Don't joke about something like that!

355
00:16:47,558 --> 00:16:49,558
There's a lot of people living in Grey Terminal.

356
00:16:49,558 --> 00:16:52,558
They can't just torch down their homes because they feel like it!

357
00:16:52,558 --> 00:16:54,558
Get off of me!

358
00:16:54,558 --> 00:16:58,558
You really are stupid. Haven't you heard a single thing I've said?

359
00:16:58,558 --> 00:17:03,558
All the shame of this country. Tomorrow they're gonna burn it all away.

360
00:17:03,558 --> 00:17:06,558
The people... too?

361
00:17:12,558 --> 00:17:14,558
Hey! Wait up!

362
00:17:16,558 --> 00:17:17,558
Where are you going?

363
00:17:21,558 --> 00:17:23,558
You can't jump out the window like that!

364
00:17:24,558 --> 00:17:30,558
Wow! He's a goner!

365
00:17:30,558 --> 00:17:32,558
It's a lie! It's gotta be!

366
00:17:32,558 --> 00:17:34,558
They can't burn down a place that big!

367
00:17:34,558 --> 00:17:36,558
And someone would've heard!

368
00:17:41,558 --> 00:17:43,558
Soldiers from this afternoon...

369
00:17:44,558 --> 00:17:46,558
Are we sure we're ready for tomorrow?

370
00:17:46,558 --> 00:17:48,558
There can't be any miscalculations!

371
00:17:48,558 --> 00:17:51,558
We're ready on our end, but we're stuck relying on the pirates.

372
00:17:51,558 --> 00:17:55,558
They have to burn the trash precisely at the right time!

373
00:17:56,558 --> 00:18:01,558
Don't worry! Blue Jam and his men have been placing boxes of oil and explosives all over Grey Terminal.

374
00:18:01,558 --> 00:18:02,558
Just like we asked.

375
00:18:04,558 --> 00:18:07,558
Blue Jam has a hand in this? It must be true!

376
00:18:07,558 --> 00:18:09,558
But why? What's in it for him?

377
00:18:09,558 --> 00:18:23,558
Hey Ace! What do you think Saba's doing?

378
00:18:23,558 --> 00:18:25,558
Seriously? Shut up!

379
00:18:25,558 --> 00:18:29,558
I thought we had agreed to stop worrying about him for now.

380
00:18:30,558 --> 00:18:31,558
Okay...

381
00:18:32,558 --> 00:18:35,558
Who knows? This could actually work out better for him.

382
00:18:35,558 --> 00:18:36,558
Saba...

383
00:18:38,558 --> 00:18:39,558
Hey Luffy!

384
00:18:39,558 --> 00:18:41,558
Where's my telescope?

385
00:18:41,558 --> 00:18:43,558
My telescope...

386
00:19:08,558 --> 00:19:09,558
Okay, think.

387
00:19:09,558 --> 00:19:11,558
If there was really going to be a fire tonight,

388
00:19:11,558 --> 00:19:14,558
the people in the town would be upset about it, right?

389
00:19:18,558 --> 00:19:19,558
Why, good morning.

390
00:19:19,558 --> 00:19:21,558
A good morning to you, sir.

391
00:19:21,558 --> 00:19:23,558
What a beautiful sunny day.

392
00:19:23,558 --> 00:19:24,558
Yes, lovely.

393
00:19:24,558 --> 00:19:25,558
What a relief.

394
00:19:25,558 --> 00:19:28,558
Guess there's nothing fishy happening today after all.

395
00:19:28,558 --> 00:19:30,558
I'll walk around for a bit.

396
00:19:30,558 --> 00:19:32,558
And just wait.

397
00:19:32,558 --> 00:19:35,558
Come tomorrow morning, things will be nicer than ever before.

398
00:19:35,558 --> 00:19:37,558
Yes, it'll be wonderful.

399
00:19:37,558 --> 00:19:47,558
It's a little breezy, but everything else here seems as normal as can be.

400
00:19:47,558 --> 00:19:51,558
Today is windy.

401
00:19:51,558 --> 00:19:55,558
That's true, your majesty. Very windy indeed.

402
00:19:55,558 --> 00:20:00,558
Accidents can happen easily on a day like this, especially wildfires.

403
00:20:00,558 --> 00:20:04,558
How right you are, majesty. It's quite possible.

404
00:20:04,558 --> 00:20:07,558
What? Sabo snuck out of the house?

405
00:20:07,558 --> 00:20:09,558
He's such an ungrateful brat.

406
00:20:09,558 --> 00:20:14,558
All he cares about is playing pirate with his friends when he should stay at home and study.

407
00:20:14,558 --> 00:20:16,558
Have the police search the entire town.

408
00:20:16,558 --> 00:20:19,558
He couldn't have gotten very far by himself.

409
00:20:19,558 --> 00:20:22,558
Um, excuse me.

410
00:20:22,558 --> 00:20:23,558
What do you want, kid?

411
00:20:23,558 --> 00:20:27,558
Did you know that there's supposed to be a fire in Great Terminal tonight?

412
00:20:27,558 --> 00:20:29,558
Of course I know about the fire.

413
00:20:29,558 --> 00:20:31,558
Why, what's wrong? Did they cancel it?

414
00:20:31,558 --> 00:20:33,558
He knows.

415
00:20:33,558 --> 00:20:35,558
Tell me, boy, whose family are you from?

416
00:20:35,558 --> 00:20:38,558
So, it's true.

417
00:20:38,558 --> 00:20:41,558
Hold on!

418
00:20:41,558 --> 00:20:44,558
Everyone knows, don't they? They have from the start!

419
00:20:44,558 --> 00:20:46,558
Look at them! They're smiling!

420
00:20:46,558 --> 00:20:49,558
They don't give a damn about the people in Great Terminal!

421
00:20:49,558 --> 00:20:52,558
They're happy to see them burned to the ground!

422
00:20:55,558 --> 00:20:58,558
You know, we've been waiting on you.

423
00:20:58,558 --> 00:21:01,558
Are there any more boxes you need us to move?

424
00:21:01,558 --> 00:21:04,558
Yeah, and I've got a bigger job for you later on.

425
00:21:04,558 --> 00:21:06,558
But we'll talk more about that tonight.

426
00:21:06,558 --> 00:21:13,558
Dad knows about it, too.

427
00:21:13,558 --> 00:21:14,558
Crap.

428
00:21:14,558 --> 00:21:17,558
That's why he brought me back home when he did.

429
00:21:17,558 --> 00:21:19,558
As much as he hates me,

430
00:21:19,558 --> 00:21:21,558
he still needs someone to inherit his property

431
00:21:21,558 --> 00:21:23,558
and maintain the family's reputation.

432
00:21:26,558 --> 00:21:28,558
Oh, sorry about that.

433
00:21:28,558 --> 00:21:30,558
He gets excited around new faces.

434
00:21:30,558 --> 00:21:32,558
Sounds to me like you're out of breath.

435
00:21:32,558 --> 00:21:33,558
Is there something bothering you?

436
00:21:33,558 --> 00:21:35,558
No, sir. It's nothing.

437
00:21:35,558 --> 00:21:36,558
Is that so?

438
00:21:36,558 --> 00:21:38,558
All right, then.

439
00:21:38,558 --> 00:21:40,558
Say, I was wondering.

440
00:21:40,558 --> 00:21:44,558
Did you know that there's supposed to be a fire going on in Great Terminal tonight?

441
00:21:44,558 --> 00:21:46,558
Yes, I heard all about the fire.

442
00:21:46,558 --> 00:21:48,558
And you're not worried? At all?

443
00:21:48,558 --> 00:21:50,558
Nobody in this town cares what happens?

444
00:21:50,558 --> 00:21:53,558
Nobody in town even thinks of stopping this thing?

445
00:21:53,558 --> 00:21:54,558
Hmm.

446
00:21:54,558 --> 00:21:59,558
That's admirable love you. You must have a very kind heart.

447
00:21:59,558 --> 00:22:02,558
But boy, please don't you say a word.

448
00:22:02,558 --> 00:22:05,558
It's important that we all keep our mouths shut.

449
00:22:05,558 --> 00:22:10,558
Think, what would happen if someone outside of Hightown found out about the plan?

450
00:22:10,558 --> 00:22:14,558
You and I are special. We come from great noble families.

451
00:22:15,558 --> 00:22:17,558
Calm down.

452
00:22:17,558 --> 00:22:21,558
Ace. Luffy. There's something wrong with this town.

453
00:22:21,558 --> 00:22:23,558
Something wrong with these people.

454
00:22:23,558 --> 00:22:33,558
They know people are going to die. They're happy people are going to die. They're sick. This whole place is sick. I can't stay here any longer. I have to tell them right now.

455
00:22:33,558 --> 00:22:39,558
Today of all days. Why is it so windy?

456
00:22:39,558 --> 00:22:42,558
That's him. That's the missing boy.

457
00:22:42,558 --> 00:22:45,558
Excuse me, kid. You need to come with us.

458
00:22:45,558 --> 00:22:47,558
Hey, you. Stop running.

459
00:22:47,558 --> 00:22:52,558
The nobles here don't care who they kill. They'll burn a whole town alive just because they don't like it.

460
00:22:52,558 --> 00:22:56,558
You've got to get out of Great Terminal and you've got to get out now.

461
00:22:56,558 --> 00:23:01,558
Hold on, Ace! Luffy! I'm coming!

462
00:23:03,558 --> 00:23:16,558
Luffy and Ace unwittingly aided Blue Jam in the plan to burn down Great Terminal and may now perish themselves.

463
00:23:16,558 --> 00:23:26,558
However, when Blue Jam runs into troubles of his own, the night descends into chaos. As the flames reach higher and higher, Sabo struggles in vain to save his friends.

464
00:23:26,558 --> 00:23:33,558
On the next, One Piece! The fire has been set! The Great Terminal in crisis! I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

